                                "text": "In decrying a decision of the court in the case of a man on trial for the larceny of a watch, the Gazette said editorially: \"Many a poor, plodding attorney in the states, when he shall read the above decision of the supreme court of Michigan, will kick his Blackstone out of his office and acknowledge himself a nincom.\" The dignity of the court could suffer no such discourtesy, and Sheldon was immediately ordered arrested for his presumption and contempt."
